Here is an example of screen scraping in Rust using the `reqwest` and `select` crates:
```
use reqwest::blocking::get;
use select::document::Document;
use select::predicate::Name;

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let res = get("https://www.example.com")?;
    let document = Document::from_read(res)?;
    let elements = document.find(Name("h1"));

    for element in elements {
        println!("{}", element.text());
    }

    Ok(())
}
```
This code sends a GET request to `https://www.example.com`, parses the HTML response using the `select` crate, and then finds all elements with the name "h1" (i.e. all `<h1>` tags). Finally, it prints the text content of each element to the console.

You'll need to add the following dependencies to your `Cargo.toml` file:
```
[dependencies]
reqwest = "0.11.6"
select = "0.5.0"
```
You can also use `async` version of `reqwest` if you want to make asynchronous requests:
```
use reqwest::Client;
use select::document::Document;
use select::predicate::Name;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let client = Client::new();
    let res = client.get("https://www.example.com").send().await?;
    let document = Document::from_read(res)?;
    let elements = document.find(Name("h1"));

    for element in elements {
        println!("{}", element.text());
    }

    Ok(())
}
```
You'll need to add the following dependencies to your `Cargo.toml` file:
```
[dependencies]
reqwest = "0.11.6"
select = "0.5.0"
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }
```
Please note that screen scraping should be done responsibly and in accordance with the website's terms of service. Also, be aware that some websites may block or limit requests from scripts, so you may need to add headers or use a user agent to mimic a real browser.

Also, you can use other libraries like `scraper` which is a rust library specifically designed for web scraping, it provides a more convenient API for scraping websites.
```
use scraper::{Html, Selector};

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let html = reqwest::blocking::get("https://www.example.com")?.text()?;
    let document = Html::parse_document(html);
    let selector = Selector::parse("h1").unwrap();
    for element in document.select(&selector) {
        println!("{}", element.text());
    }

    Ok(())
}
```
You'll need to add the following dependencies to your `Cargo.toml` file:
```
[dependencies]
reqwest = "0.11.6"
scraper = "0.12.0"
```
Please let me know if you have any questions or need further assistance.

